# The assessment of AGT-EXEC-002 against this build. The requirement identifier is this
# file's stem and appears nowhere inside it, because a second place to spell the identity
# is a second place for it to be wrong -- the rule OD-SPEC-007 chose for a record
# registration, and CHK-003.assessment states for this registry.
#
# AGT-EXEC-002: "Agent runs shall declare filesystem scope, network policy, executable
# allowlist, secret access, environment variables, process limits, model-provider/
# data-retention policy, and maximum patch/artifact size." Eight declared dimensions.
#
# `Territory` (nomos-scope-verification, reused by nomos-ledger) already declares the
# first: an item's `paths` name exactly what a claiming agent's run is scoped to touch,
# checked for overlap against every other claim before either may proceed. It is a real,
# tested, load-bearing declaration -- not an
# aspiration -- and it is what an agent's own run is bound by in this workspace today,
# since claiming and working a ledger item is the concrete shape an "agent run" already
# takes here.
#
# The other seven -- network policy, executable allowlist, secret access, environment
# variables, process limits, model-provider/data-retention policy, maximum patch/artifact
# size -- have no declared shape anywhere. `Claim`, the type that actually represents one
# agent holding one run, carries only who holds it and when the lease lapses; nothing about
# what that run may reach beyond its territory.
verdict: Partial
site: crates/substrate/nomos-scope-verification/src/territory.rs#Territory
gap: crates/substrate/nomos-ledger/src/claim.rs#Claim
